   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc117674206"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc249769_2093603017"/>Introduction<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc117674206"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc249769_2093603017"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P88">The OpenCPI On Chip Control Plane (OCCP) memory allocation handles memory in a specific way when deploy<text:span text:style-name="T74">ing</text:span> on <text:span text:style-name="T75">a </text:span>platform. This document is written for developers explaining how memory is allocated, the <text:span text:style-name="T75">memory </text:span>addressing is done, <text:span text:style-name="T75">how configurations can be altered, </text:span>and the limits imposed when <text:span text:style-name="T75">executing an OpenCPI application that uses</text:span> a <text:span text:style-name="T75">hardware description language (HDL)</text:span> assembl<text:span text:style-name="T75">y.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P74" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc3467690_2093603017"/>References<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc3467690_2093603017"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P6">The d<text:span text:style-name="T75">ocument currently has no references.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9">Table <text:sequence text:ref-name="refTable0" text:name="Table" text:formula="ooow:1 " style:num-format="1">1</text:sequence>: <text:s/>Table of Reference Documents</text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table18" table:style-name="Table18">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table18.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table18.B"/>
